{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nids=['hyp-20260923-001-r4s0','hyp-20260923-001-r6s0','hyp-20260923-001-r7s0','hyp-20260923-002-r8s1']\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n x=json.loads(line)\n if x.get('id') in ids:\n  print('\\\\nID',x['id'])\n  print('hypothesis',x['hypothesis']['hypothesis'] if isinstance(x['hypothesis'],dict) else x['hypothesis'])\n  print('notes',x.get('implementation_notes',''))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nids=['hyp-20260923-001-r4s0','hyp-20260923-001-r6s0','hyp-20260923-001-r7s0','hyp-20260923-002-r8s1']\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n x=json.loads(line)\n if x.get('id') in ids:\n  print('\\\\nID',x['id'])\n  print('hypothesis',x['hypothesis']['hypothesis'] if isinstance(x['hypothesis'],dict) else x['hypothesis'])\n  print('notes',x.get('implementation_notes',''))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"\nID hyp-20260923-001-r4s0\nhypothesis Decode the legal ALU operation to one-hot selects in ID and register those\nselects with the existing ID/EX payload. In EX, compute the RV32I arithmetic,\nlogical, shift, and multiply candidates in parallel and select them with\nthe registered one-hot bits, avoiding a five-bit operation decode after the\nID/EX register. Retain the encoded operation for the divider handshake and\npreserve both real RV32M results and RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS substitutions.\nKeep the existing forwarding, stall, trap, retirement, and nret=1 behavior.\nRemoving EX decode depth should improve Fmax with the same timed cycle count.\n\nnotes \n\nID hyp-20260923-001-r6s0\nhypothesis Make load-use and redirect bubbles invalidate only the ID/EX valid bit and\nthe three controls that can affect memory or forwarding: mem_read,\nmem_write, and reg_write. Let the remaining payload capture its normal\ndecoded values on a bubble; those values cannot cause architectural\neffects while valid is zero and the side-effect controls are clear. Keep\nfull reset behavior. Give dmem and divide holds priority over a bubble,\nwhile retaining the existing PC hold on load-use. This removes the hazard\nresult from the wide ID/EX data-register reset/enable network and should\nimprove Fmax without changing the retirement cycle count, RVFI sequence,\nor bus-stall behavior.\n\nnotes \n\nID hyp-20260923-001-r7s0\nhypothesis Split ID/EX storage so reset clears valid and the complete control word,\nwhile PC, instruction, register operands and addresses, immediate, destination,\nand one-hot ALU select flops have no reset input. Keep their normal capture\nand hold behavior, including the existing bubble rule that clears valid and\nmemory/writeback side-effect controls. An invalid ID/EX entry must still\nproduce no redirect, divide launch, memory request, register write, or\nretirement; the reset control word provides that guard until a real fetch is\ncaptured. This should remove a reset mux and high-fanout reset routing from\nthe wide decode destination without adding cycles or a new EX bypass path.\n\nnotes \n\nID hyp-20260923-002-r8s1\nhypothesis For validated BRANCH and JAL instructions, register PC plus the decoded\nimmediate in the existing ID/EX immediate field. Keep the raw immediate\nfor JALR, loads, stores, and arithmetic. EX will use the registered\nabsolute target for BRANCH and JAL, while retaining its forwarded-rs1\nplus immediate computation for JALR. Preserve EX branch-condition and\nalignment checks, redirect priority, link writeback, RVFI next-PC and\ntrap fields, and all bus-stall behavior. This removes the PC-relative\ntarget adder from EX-to-IF redirect and EX/MEM result timing with no\nCoreMark cycle penalty or additional target mux in fetch. The ID path\ngains an adder, so the Fmax benefit is uncertain but directly testable.\n\nnotes \n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
