{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260923-001-r10s0.yaml')\nprint('exists',p.exists())\nprint(p.read_text())\ntry:\n import yaml, json, jsonschema\n doc=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\n schema=json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json'))\n jsonschema.validate(doc,schema)\n print('schema_valid',True)\nexcept ImportError as e:\n print('validation_modules_unavailable',e)\nexcept Exception as e:\n print('schema_valid',False,type(e).__name__,e)\n raise\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"exists True\nid: hyp-20260923-001-r10s0\ntitle: \"Use one-hot EX operand forwarding selects\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  Each EX operand passes through a forwarding priority encoder followed by a\n  three-way data mux before reaching the ALU or branch comparator. This path\n  affects common dependent instructions and the branch redirect path. The\n  earlier registered one-hot ALU select improved fitness by removing decode\n  depth from EX; forwarding offers a similar, smaller timing opportunity.\nhypothesis: |\n  Generate mutually exclusive one-hot forwarding selects directly from the\n  existing EX/MEM and MEM/WB register-address comparisons. Give EX/MEM the\n  same priority over MEM/WB, and select each 32-bit operand with parallel\n  masks and an OR reduction instead of encoding a two-bit choice and decoding\n  it again in EX. Keep the MEM/WB comparison active when its valid bit is\n  cleared by a dmem stall, since the retained value is required by a held\n  dependent instruction. Preserve x0 exclusion, the load-use interlock, all\n  bus and divide holds, and the single-retirement RVFI behavior. CoreMark\n  cycles should remain unchanged; a shorter forwarding-to-ALU and\n  forwarding-to-branch path may improve routed Fmax.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: \"Output mutually exclusive one-hot selects for each source, preserving EX/MEM priority, MEM/WB fallback, and x0 exclusion.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Replace each encoded forwarding case mux with a parallel masked-OR operand selection using the new one-hot bits.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Widen the forwarding-select wires and connect the one-hot forward unit to EX without changing top-level ports.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Check EX/MEM versus MEM/WB priority, x0 reads, dependent branches, and a held MEM/WB value across repeated dmem stalls.\"\n\nschema_valid True\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
