{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -c \"python3 -c 'import json; p=\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\"; xs=[json.loads(l) for l in open(p)]; [print(x[\\\"id\\\"],\\\"\\\\n\\\",x[\\\"hypothesis\\\"][\\\"hypothesis\\\"],\\\"\\\\n\\\",x.get(\\\"lesson\\\",\\\"\\\")) for x in xs if x.get(\\\"category\\\")==\\\"micro_opt\\\" and any(s in x[\\\"id\\\"] for s in (\\\"r7s0\\\",\\\"r9s0\\\"))]'\"","aggregated_output":"hyp-20260923-001-r7s0 \n Split ID/EX storage so reset clears valid and the complete control word,\nwhile PC, instruction, register operands and addresses, immediate, destination,\nand one-hot ALU select flops have no reset input. Keep their normal capture\nand hold behavior, including the existing bubble rule that clears valid and\nmemory/writeback side-effect controls. An invalid ID/EX entry must still\nproduce no redirect, divide launch, memory request, register write, or\nretirement; the reset control word provides that guard until a real fetch is\ncaptured. This should remove a reset mux and high-fanout reset routing from\nthe wide decode destination without adding cycles or a new EX bypass path.\n \n \nhyp-20260923-001-r9s0 \n Pass the raw imem instruction through IF/ID every cycle and use IF/ID.valid\nto mark unavailable or wrong-path fetches. In ID, continue to capture the\nordinary payload, but force valid, mem_read, mem_write, and reg_write low\nfor an invalid fetch or a flush. In the hazard unit, qualify load-use\ndetection with IF/ID.valid so arbitrary instruction bits during a redirect\nor imem stall cannot hold the PC. EX already qualifies redirects and divide\nlaunches with validity. This removes the flush/redirect NOP mux from the\ninstruction-to-register-file path without adding a stage, changing cycle\nbehavior, or allowing an invalid instruction to access memory or retire.\nKeep decoder default-illegal behavior and all RVFI and bus-stall checks.\n \n \n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
