{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/zsh -c \"rg -n 'critical|timing|path|mul|ALU|adder|comparator' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | tail -5\"", "aggregated_output": "30:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260923-002-r10s1\", \"title\": \"Eliminate the divider's duplicate pipeline register\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The iterative divider was the strongest structural improvement so far, but\\nEX still captures a full EX/MEM bundle in div_meta_q when a divide starts.\\nID/EX already remains held throughout the divide, so most of that duplicate\\nregister stores metadata that is still available at completion. It adds\\nflip-flops, routing, and an EX result path even though CoreMark rarely divides.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The iterative divider was the strongest structural improvement so far, but\\nEX still captures a full EX/MEM bundle in div_meta_q when a divide starts.\\nID/EX already remains held throughout the divide, so most of that duplicate\\nregister stores metadata that is still available at completion. It adds\\nflip-flops, routing, and an EX result path even though CoreMark rarely divides.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Remove the full-width div_meta_q register. At divider launch, retain only\\nthe two post-forwarding source values needed for exact RVFI rs1/rs2 data;\\nthe divider continues to capture its arithmetic operands as today. While\\ndivision runs or its completed result waits for dmem backpressure, keep\\nID/EX held. On the accepting edge, construct one EX/MEM divide entry from\\nthe held ID/EX PC, instruction, addresses, destination and controls, the\\nsaved source values, div_result, and PC+4. Set branch-only and unused store\\nfields to zero. Let older work drain and emit invalid EX/MEM bubbles during\\nthe wait, exactly as in the current interlock. This removes a wide duplicate\\nstage register and its input logic without adding a CoreMark cycle or a mux\\nto the ordinary fetch and ALU paths. Preserve the existing real and ALTOPS\\ndivider behavior, ordered nret=1 retirement, and all stall priorities.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace div_meta_q with launch-captured forwarded rs1/rs2 v\n…[18612 of 21684 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:85749af8afc9e5f9]…\nthe prediction with its instruction and clear it on invalid or flushed decode entries.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Suppress the EX redirect for a correctly predicted direct JAL while preserving its architectural target, link register write, trap behavior, and RVFI next PC.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Connect the accepted-fetch prediction to the existing single-retire pipeline without changing top-level ports.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Check eligible and ineligible JALs, page crossings, misalignment, wrong-path suppression, bus stalls, link values, and RVFI PC/order.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 330.62, \"delta_pct\": -19.08, \"vs_baseline\": 16.9, \"fmax_mhz\": 146.93, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4444081, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5688, \"ff\": 2213, \"seeds\": [146.93, 134.81, 161.81], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-23T19:13:20.273201Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 11}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
