{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_2", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/zsh -c \"rg -n '\\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\"|micro_opt' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | tail -45\"", "aggregated_output": "1:{\"id\": \"baseline-bench-693038e\", \"title\": \"Baseline retest for cores/bench\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 282.82, \"delta_pct\": 0.0, \"vs_baseline\": 0.0, \"fmax_mhz\": 127.03, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 9563, \"ff\": 1866, \"seeds\": [128.72, 127.03, 123.02], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-23T15:32:48.790916Z\", \"round_id\": 0, \"slot\": 0}\n2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260923-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Forward live MEM load data into EX\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The in-order pipeline inserts a bubble whenever an instruction immediately\\nconsumes a load result, even though the zero-wait memory model presents that\\nresult combinationally while the load is in MEM. CoreMark's list and matrix\\ncode repeatedly loads a value before using it. Removing these bubbles should\\nimprove iterations per cycle without changing the retirement width.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The in-order pipeline inserts a bubble whenever an instruction immediately\\nconsumes a load result, even though the zero-wait memory model presents that\\nresult combinationally while the load is in MEM. CoreMark's list and matrix\\ncode repeatedly loads a value before using it. Removing these bubbles should\\nimprove iterations per cycle without changing the retirement width.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a MEM-to-EX bypass for the current load's fully extracted and extended\\ndata, and let the dependent instruction enter EX directly behind the load.\\nWhen dmem is not ready, hold both instructions until the response is valid;\\nsuppress EX redirects during that hold. Do not forward a misaligned load\\nthat traps. Keep the existing EX/MEM priority for ordinary ALU results and\\nthe MEM/WB fallback for older writers. The bypass should reduce load-use\\nstalls while preserving RVFI operand values and exact memory semantics.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.\n…[41358 of 44430 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:f18103498bf0b373]…\nrtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the same sliced PC+4 increment for link writeback and fall-through or trapping RVFI next PC, without changing branch or JALR target arithmetic.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Check PC+4 carry propagation across slice boundaries, wraparound, links and RVFI next PCs, including redirects and bus stalls.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 382.38, \"delta_pct\": -6.41, \"vs_baseline\": 35.2, \"fmax_mhz\": 171.76, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491817, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5713, \"ff\": 2201, \"seeds\": [171.76, 175.59, 170.47], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-23T19:31:57.358863Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 12, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-23 hyp-20260923-001-r12s0 (regression, -6.41%): Splitting IF and EX PC+4 into eight-bit adders with wide prefix-AND carry enables can map worse than a native constant adder on FPGA, reducing fitness when CoreMark cycle count has no reason to change.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
