{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260923-001-r14s0.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260923-001-r14s0\ntitle: \"Share the ALU right-shift barrel network\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The one-hot ALU currently builds separate 32-bit logical and arithmetic\n  right shifters, then masks both results into the final OR tree. Both shifts\n  use the same data and shift amount; only the fill bit differs. Earlier\n  datapath sharing attempts put an operation mux ahead of arithmetic and\n  lowered Fmax, so this change targets the common shift network without\n  adding a mux to the data or shift-amount inputs.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the separate SRL and SRA expressions in alu.sv with one signed\n  33-bit arithmetic right shift. Form its input as\n  {sel[ALU_SRA] & a[31], a}; the extra sign bit is zero for SRL and copies\n  a[31] for SRA. Mask the low 32 result bits once with\n  sel[ALU_SRL] | sel[ALU_SRA] in the existing one-hot result OR tree.\n  This should remove one barrel network and one wide output mask while\n  preserving exact RV32IM shift results for every shift amount. Keep all\n  other ALU operations, ALTOPS substitutions, pipeline timing, and RVFI\n  behavior unchanged. Fewer shift LUTs and shorter result selection may\n  improve routed Fmax at the same CoreMark cycle count.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 2\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Use one sign-fill-controlled right shifter for SRL and SRA and one result-mask term; leave other ALU operations intact.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Add SRL/SRA vectors for negative and positive operands at shift amounts 0, 1, 15, and 31, checking exact 32-bit results.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
