{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_3", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/zsh -c \"rg -n 'micro_opt|fmax_mhz|coremark_iter_s|fitness|hyp-20260923-001-r14s0' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | tail -n 25\"", "aggregated_output": "19:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260923-003-r6s2\", \"title\": \"Predict one hot backward branch with registered lookahead\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"Earlier branch predictors removed about 4 to 6 percent of CoreMark cycles,\\nbut their fetch lookup, target arithmetic, or full-width EX recovery check\\nreduced Fmax enough to lose fitness. The current core reaches 176.15 MHz,\\nso a predictor must keep both the IF PC selection and EX redirect short.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Earlier branch predictors removed about 4 to 6 percent of CoreMark cycles,\\nbut their fetch lookup, target arithmetic, or full-width EX recovery check\\nreduced Fmax enough to lose fitness. The current core reaches 176.15 MHz,\\nso a predictor must keep both the IF PC selection and EX redirect short.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add one entry for a repeatedly taken conditional branch with a negative\\nB-type offset. Store its branch PC minus four, B-immediate signature, and\\nresolved aligned target. When an accepted sequential fetch PC matches the\\nstored predecessor PC, register the target and signature as lookahead for\\nthe next fetch. On that next fetch, predict taken only if the delivered\\ninstruction is a legal BRANCH with the same B-immediate bits; otherwise\\ncontinue at PC+4. The exact sequential predecessor match establishes the\\nbranch PC, and the immediate match establishes the target, so EX needs only\\na predicted-taken bit, not a predicted 32-bit PC or target comparison.\\n\\nIn EX, compare that bit with the resolved taken outcome after misalignment\\nhandling. Redirect to the resolved target or PC+4 only on a direction\\nmismatch, using the existing same-cycle recovery path. Train once when a\\nvalid aligned taken branch advances from EX; do not train or redirect while\\nEX is held. Hold lookahead during bus or decode stalls and invalidate it on\\nany nonsequential PC change. This should retain useful loop predictions\\nwhile avoiding the timing costs seen in the larger and full-PC predictors.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidenc\n…[108123 of 111195 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b6ab5c8b535f685d]…\nn; repair untaken, illegal, long-offset, block-crossing, or trapping guesses using the resolved next PC.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Check short taken loops, untaken exits, block boundaries, long negative offsets, illegal and misaligned branches, stalls, wrong-path side effects, and RVFI PC and order.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 435.24, \"delta_pct\": 6.53, \"vs_baseline\": 53.89, \"fmax_mhz\": 188.61, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4333465, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5713, \"ff\": 2209, \"seeds\": [174.52, 188.61, 190.62], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-23T21:08:02.280529Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 14, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-23 hyp-20260923-003-r14s2 (improvement, +6.53%): For backward-branch prediction, muxing only PC[7:0] in IF and checking offset size and block carry from registered metadata in EX preserves CoreMark cycle savings while avoiding the fetch-PC timing penalty of live eligibility checks.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
