{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/zsh -c \"rg -n 'critical path|worst path|timing|RF-to|register-file-to|multiplier' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | tail -n 12 | cut -c1-500\"", "aggregated_output": "26:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260923-001-r9s0\", \"title\": \"Remove the invalid-fetch NOP mux from register-file reads\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"Prior routed analysis identified the live instruction-input to ID/EX\\nregister-file read as a critical path. The current IF stage selects a NOP\\nahead of every instruction bit when fetch is invalid or EX redirects, so\\neven the source-register addresses traverse that mux before the 32-entry\\nregister-file read. Earlier register-file banking and EX retim\n28:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260923-003-r9s2\", \"title\": \"Predict branch direction at execute to shorten PC steering\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"Earlier fetch-side predictors saved roughly four to six percent of CoreMark\\ncycles but lost more fitness to added fetch-PC and recovery timing. The\\ncurrent EX branch comparison also feeds the same-cycle redirect path.\\nPredicting only the branch decision at the existing EX redirect point\\navoids a target table, live fetch decode, and another normal f\n29:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260923-001-r10s0\", \"title\": \"Use one-hot EX operand forwarding selects\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"Each EX operand passes through a forwarding priority encoder followed by a\\nthree-way data mux before reaching the ALU or branch comparator. This path\\naffects common dependent instructions and the branch redirect path. The\\nearlier registered one-hot ALU select improved fitness by removing decode\\ndepth from EX; forwarding offers a similar, smaller timing opportunity\n32:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260923-001-r11s0\", \"title\": \"Select narrow load lanes without a word shifter\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The MEM load path