{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category')=='micro_opt' and d['id'].endswith(('r9s0','r13s0')):\n  print('\\\\n',d['id'],d['title'])\n  print(d['hypothesis']['motivation'])\n  print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"\n hyp-20260923-001-r9s0 Remove the invalid-fetch NOP mux from register-file reads\nPrior routed analysis identified the live instruction-input to ID/EX\nregister-file read as a critical path. The current IF stage selects a NOP\nahead of every instruction bit when fetch is invalid or EX redirects, so\neven the source-register addresses traverse that mux before the 32-entry\nregister-file read. Earlier register-file banking and EX retiming reduced\nfitness; removing this existing input mux is a smaller change to that path.\n\nPass the raw imem instruction through IF/ID every cycle and use IF/ID.valid\nto mark unavailable or wrong-path fetches. In ID, continue to capture the\nordinary payload, but force valid, mem_read, mem_write, and reg_write low\nfor an invalid fetch or a flush. In the hazard unit, qualify load-use\ndetection with IF/ID.valid so arbitrary instruction bits during a redirect\nor imem stall cannot hold the PC. EX already qualifies redirects and divide\nlaunches with validity. This removes the flush/redirect NOP mux from the\ninstruction-to-register-file path without adding a stage, changing cycle\nbehavior, or allowing an invalid instruction to access memory or retire.\nKeep decoder default-illegal behavior and all RVFI and bus-stall checks.\n\n\n hyp-20260923-001-r13s0 Latch branch funct3 without opcode gating\nA routed bench timing report ends at an ID/EX branch_op bit after several\nlevels of instruction decode and control muxing. The branch selector is\nmeaningful only when is_branch is asserted, yet the decoder currently\ndrives it through a validated BRANCH opcode case and a default value.\nEarlier attempts that added work to fetch or forwarding reduced Fmax;\nremoving this decode gate targets the measured ID register path directly.\n\nDrive branch_op directly from instr[14:12] for every instruction, while\nretaining the existing validated opcode/funct3 logic for is_branch and\nis_illegal. EX already qualifies branch_taken with is_branch, so raw\nfunct3 from non-branches or reserved branch encodings cannot redirect\nthe PC. Keep all other controls, stage boundaries, bus holds, RVFI fields,\nand the nret=1 interface unchanged. This removes the opcode and legality\nmux from the instruction-to-ID/EX branch selector path without adding a\ncycle or logic to the fetch PC path, potentially raising routed Fmax.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
