{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_3", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/zsh -c \"rg -n 'micro_opt|hyp-20260923|fitness|notes' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "1:{\"id\": \"baseline-bench-693038e\", \"title\": \"Baseline retest for cores/bench\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 282.82, \"delta_pct\": 0.0, \"vs_baseline\": 0.0, \"fmax_mhz\": 127.03, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 9563, \"ff\": 1866, \"seeds\": [128.72, 127.03, 123.02], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-23T15:32:48.790916Z\", \"round_id\": 0, \"slot\": 0}\n2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260923-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Forward live MEM load data into EX\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The in-order pipeline inserts a bubble whenever an instruction immediately\\nconsumes a load result, even though the zero-wait memory model presents that\\nresult combinationally while the load is in MEM. CoreMark's list and matrix\\ncode repeatedly loads a value before using it. Removing these bubbles should\\nimprove iterations per cycle without changing the retirement width.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The in-order pipeline inserts a bubble whenever an instruction immediately\\nconsumes a load result, even though the zero-wait memory model presents that\\nresult combinationally while the load is in MEM. CoreMark's list and matrix\\ncode repeatedly loads a value before using it. Removing these bubbles should\\nimprove iterations per cycle without changing the retirement width.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a MEM-to-EX bypass for the current load's fully extracted and extended\\ndata, and let the dependent instruction enter EX directly behind the load.\\nWhen dmem is not ready, hold both instructions until the response is valid;\\nsuppress EX redirects during that hold. Do not forward a misaligned load\\nthat traps. Keep the existing EX/MEM priority for ordinary ALU results and\\nthe MEM/WB fallback for older writers. The bypass should reduce load-use\\nstalls while preserving RVFI operand values and exact memory semantics.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.\n…[12254 of 15326 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:d1d68caa792f5606]…\n_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Flush younger instructions only on misprediction and defer recovery while EX is held by a dmem stall.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Exercise repeated taken and untaken branches, JAL and changing JALR targets, wrong-path suppression, and recovery with instruction and data bus stalls; check RVFI order and PCs.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 348.08, \"delta_pct\": 23.07, \"vs_baseline\": 23.07, \"fmax_mhz\": 147.38, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4234052, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10412, \"ff\": 2076, \"seeds\": [130.34, 148.68, 147.38], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-23T15:52:38.410593Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-23 hyp-20260923-003-r1s2 (regression, +23.07%): A 16-entry tagged fetch BTB saved roughly 6% of CoreMark cycles, but its 10,412 LUT4 footprint exceeded the 10,000-LUT4 target and its 147.4 MHz Fmax left it just behind the iterative divider's fitness.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
