{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/zsh -c \"rg -n 'mul|MUL|critical path|timing|fmax|carry|adder' cores/*/LESSONS.md cores/*/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:1:{\"id\": \"baseline-bench-693038e\", \"title\": \"Baseline retest for cores/bench\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 282.82, \"delta_pct\": 0.0, \"vs_baseline\": 0.0, \"fmax_mhz\": 127.03, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 9563, \"ff\": 1866, \"seeds\": [128.72, 127.03, 123.02], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-23T15:32:48.790916Z\", \"round_id\": 0, \"slot\": 0}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260923-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Forward live MEM load data into EX\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The in-order pipeline inserts a bubble whenever an instruction immediately\\nconsumes a load result, even though the zero-wait memory model presents that\\nresult combinationally while the load is in MEM. CoreMark's list and matrix\\ncode repeatedly loads a value before using it. Removing these bubbles should\\nimprove iterations per cycle without changing the retirement width.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The in-order pipeline inserts a bubble whenever an instruction immediately\\nconsumes a load result, even though the zero-wait memory model presents that\\nresult combinationally while the load is in MEM. CoreMark's list and matrix\\ncode repeatedly loads a value before using it. Removing these bubbles should\\nimprove iterations per cycle without changing the retirement width.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a MEM-to-EX bypass for the current load's fully extracted and extended\\ndata, and let the dependent instruction enter EX directly behind the load.\\nWhen dmem is not ready, hold both instructions until the response is valid;\\nsuppress EX redirects during that hold. Do not forward a misaligned load\\nthat traps. Keep the existing EX/MEM priority for ordinary ALU results and\\nthe MEM/WB fallback for older writers. The bypass should reduce load-use\\nstalls while preserving RVFI operand values and exact memory semantics.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pc\n…[609877 of 612949 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:8b7d9b4af89fd6c7]…\nFI `mem_rdata` use the cached raw word.\\n- Legal normal-RAM stores invalidate a matching replay entry when they retire directly or enqueue into the pending-store slot.\\n\\n## Deviations\\n\\n- Store byte-merge updating was not implemented; matching stores invalidate the latch conservatively as proposed.\\n- The helper uses a 30-bit word-address input rather than a 32-bit byte address to avoid unused low-bit logic and lint warnings.\\n\\n## Concerns\\n\\n- The direct command `bash formal/run_all.sh` could not stage files in this sandbox because `formal/riscv-formal` points outside the writable worktree area and its core staging directory rejects writes. The same script was run from a `/tmp` mirror of the current RTL and formal harness instead.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv rtl/*.sv`: pass.\\n- Formal self-check from `/tmp/llr_formal.g2j1qf` using the same `formal/run_all.sh`: pass, `105 passed, 0 failed`.\\n\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-28T13:30:43.017656\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 25}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
