{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_1", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/zsh -c \"rg -n 'micro_opt|hyp-20260923-001-r2s0|hyp-20260923-001-r3s0' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "1:{\"id\": \"baseline-bench-693038e\", \"title\": \"Baseline retest for cores/bench\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 282.82, \"delta_pct\": 0.0, \"vs_baseline\": 0.0, \"fmax_mhz\": 127.03, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 9563, \"ff\": 1866, \"seeds\": [128.72, 127.03, 123.02], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-23T15:32:48.790916Z\", \"round_id\": 0, \"slot\": 0}\n2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260923-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Forward live MEM load data into EX\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The in-order pipeline inserts a bubble whenever an instruction immediately\\nconsumes a load result, even though the zero-wait memory model presents that\\nresult combinationally while the load is in MEM. CoreMark's list and matrix\\ncode repeatedly loads a value before using it. Removing these bubbles should\\nimprove iterations per cycle without changing the retirement width.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The in-order pipeline inserts a bubble whenever an instruction immediately\\nconsumes a load result, even though the zero-wait memory model presents that\\nresult combinationally while the load is in MEM. CoreMark's list and matrix\\ncode repeatedly loads a value before using it. Removing these bubbles should\\nimprove iterations per cycle without changing the retirement width.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a MEM-to-EX bypass for the current load's fully extracted and extended\\ndata, and let the dependent instruction enter EX directly behind the load.\\nWhen dmem is not ready, hold both instructions until the response is valid;\\nsuppress EX redirects during that hold. Do not forward a misaligned load\\nthat traps. Keep the existing EX/MEM priority for ordinary ALU results and\\nthe MEM/WB fallback for older writers. The bypass should reduce load-use\\nstalls while preserving RVFI operand values and exact memory semantics.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.\n…[7470 of 10542 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:39e56253adf7de99]…\niption\": \"Derive the quotient decision and next remainder from one widened subtract, accounting for trial[32] when the shifted remainder exceeds 32 bits.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_div_unit.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed high-bit trial, divide-by-zero, and signed-edge vectors to check the shared subtract across all four divide and remainder operations.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 341.4, \"delta_pct\": -5.68, \"vs_baseline\": 20.71, \"fmax_mhz\": 153.35, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491817, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5569, \"ff\": 2169, \"seeds\": [153.35, 160.15, 153.28], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-23T16:25:10.956026Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 3, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-23 hyp-20260923-001-r3s0 (regression, -5.68%): Sharing the divider's comparison and difference through a 33-bit subtraction makes the restoring decision depend on its borrow carry chain; with the same 32 steps, this arithmetic saving can worsen FPGA fitness.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
