{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/zsh -c \"rg -n 'critical|timing|reg_file|branch|mul|shift|fmax|frequency' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | tail -12\"", "aggregated_output": "1:{\"id\": \"baseline-bench-693038e\", \"title\": \"Baseline retest for cores/bench\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 282.82, \"delta_pct\": 0.0, \"vs_baseline\": 0.0, \"fmax_mhz\": 127.03, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 9563, \"ff\": 1866, \"seeds\": [128.72, 127.03, 123.02], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-23T15:32:48.790916Z\", \"round_id\": 0, \"slot\": 0}\n2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260923-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Forward live MEM load data into EX\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The in-order pipeline inserts a bubble whenever an instruction immediately\\nconsumes a load result, even though the zero-wait memory model presents that\\nresult combinationally while the load is in MEM. CoreMark's list and matrix\\ncode repeatedly loads a value before using it. Removing these bubbles should\\nimprove iterations per cycle without changing the retirement width.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The in-order pipeline inserts a bubble whenever an instruction immediately\\nconsumes a load result, even though the zero-wait memory model presents that\\nresult combinationally while the load is in MEM. CoreMark's list and matrix\\ncode repeatedly loads a value before using it. Removing these bubbles should\\nimprove iterations per cycle without changing the retirement width.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a MEM-to-EX bypass for the current load's fully extracted and extended\\ndata, and let the dependent instruction enter EX directly behind the load.\\nWhen dmem is not ready, hold both instructions until the response is valid;\\nsuppress EX redirects during that hold. Do not forward a misaligned load\\nthat traps. Keep the existing EX/MEM priority for ordinary ALU results and\\nthe MEM/WB fallback for older writers. The bypass should reduce load-use\\nstalls while preserving RVFI operand values and exact memory semantics.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.\n…[38032 of 41104 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:36d7fd943cc33825]…\n acceptance, and misprediction recovery to fetch while preserving the nret=1 top-level interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Check warmed taken and untaken branches, direct jumps, JALR fallback, aliased counters, illegal branch encodings, misaligned targets, bus stalls, and RVFI PC/order correctness.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 348.78, \"delta_pct\": -3.64, \"vs_baseline\": 23.32, \"fmax_mhz\": 146.61, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4203461, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5893, \"ff\": 2243, \"seeds\": [145.71, 153.96, 146.61], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-23T16:28:09.698339Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 3, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-23 hyp-20260923-003-r3s2 (regression, -3.64%): A 32-entry direction table saved roughly 6% of CoreMark cycles, but same-cycle B/J predecode, counter lookup, and PC-plus-immediate target selection in IF coincided with Fmax falling from 162.58 to 146.6 MHz, outweighing the cycle gain.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
