{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor s in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(s)\n if d.get('category')=='micro_opt':\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  if isinstance(h,dict): h=h.get('hypothesis','')\n  print('\\\\n',d['id'],d.get('outcome'),d.get('title')); print(h[:1100])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"\n baseline-bench-693038e improvement Baseline retest for cores/bench\n\n\n hyp-20260923-001-r1s0 regression Forward live MEM load data into EX\nAdd a MEM-to-EX bypass for the current load's fully extracted and extended\ndata, and let the dependent instruction enter EX directly behind the load.\nWhen dmem is not ready, hold both instructions until the response is valid;\nsuppress EX redirects during that hold. Do not forward a misaligned load\nthat traps. Keep the existing EX/MEM priority for ordinary ALU results and\nthe MEM/WB fallback for older writers. The bypass should reduce load-use\nstalls while preserving RVFI operand values and exact memory semantics.\n\n\n hyp-20260923-001-r2s0 improvement Segment the RVFI retirement order counter\nReplace the single 64-bit increment in core.sv with four 16-bit counter\nchunks. Increment the low chunk whenever mem_wb_w.valid retires. Increment\neach higher chunk on that same retirement only when all lower chunks are\n16'hffff before the clock edge. Concatenate the chunks to drive the existing\nio_rvfi_order_0 port and reset every chunk to zero. This preserves the exact\n64-bit sequence, including carries and wraparound, while giving synthesis\nshorter local incrementers instead of one wide carry chain. Keep retirement\ntiming, the nret=1 port set, and all other RVFI fields unchanged.\n\n\n hyp-20260923-001-r3s0 regression Share the divider comparison and subtraction\nCompute one 33-bit subtraction of the low 32 bits of the trial remainder\nand the divisor. Use its borrow bit, together with trial[32], to decide\nwhether subtraction succeeds; use the low 32 result bits as the candidate\nremainder. This replaces the separate wide comparison and subtraction\nwhile preserving all 32 restoring steps, the existing EX interlock, and\nexact DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU results. Keep divide-by-zero, signed correction,\ncompletion holding, and the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS branch unchanged. Reduced\nduplicated arithmetic and routing should improve FPGA Fmax with identical\nCoreMark cycles.\n\n\n hyp-20260923-001-r4s0 improvement Register one-hot ALU selects before execute\nDecode the legal ALU operation to one-hot selects in ID and register those\nselects with the existing ID/EX payload. In EX, compute the RV32I arithmetic,\nlogical, shift, and multiply candidates in parallel and select them with\nthe registered one-hot bits, avoiding a five-bit operation decode after the\nID/EX register. Retain the encoded operation for the divider handshake and\npreserve both real RV32M results and RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS substitutions.\nKeep the existing forwarding, stall, trap, retirement, and nret=1 behavior.\nRemoving EX decode depth should improve Fmax with the same timed cycle count.\n\n\n hyp-20260923-001-r5s0 regression Bank the register-file read muxes\nKeep the same 32 x 32 flip-flop register array and synchronous write port,\nbut implement each asynchronous read as four local eight-register banks.\nDecode the low three address bits once per read port into one-hot selects,\nOR the selected register within each bank, then select one of the four bank\nresults with the high two address bits. Keep x0 hardwired to zero and retain\nthe existing same-cycle WB write-through priority. This bounded local read\nnetwork should map to fewer serial LUT and routing levels on the measured\ninstruction-to-ID/EX operand path, improving median Fmax while preserving\nthe single-issue retirement stream and all RVFI values.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
