{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260923-001-r6s0.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260923-001-r6s0\ntitle: \"Clear only side-effect controls on ID/EX bubbles\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current load-use interlock clears the entire ID/EX bundle, making a\n  live instruction-bit comparison control more than 200 register inputs.\n  A fresh route of the present RTL has its critical path from an instruction\n  bit through this hazard logic to an ID/EX register. Earlier register-file\n  banking worsened this fetch-to-decode path, so shortening bubble control\n  without changing the read mux is the more focused opportunity.\nhypothesis: |\n  Make load-use and redirect bubbles invalidate only the ID/EX valid bit and\n  the three controls that can affect memory or forwarding: mem_read,\n  mem_write, and reg_write. Let the remaining payload capture its normal\n  decoded values on a bubble; those values cannot cause architectural\n  effects while valid is zero and the side-effect controls are clear. Keep\n  full reset behavior. Give dmem and divide holds priority over a bubble,\n  while retaining the existing PC hold on load-use. This removes the hazard\n  result from the wide ID/EX data-register reset/enable network and should\n  improve Fmax without changing the retirement cycle count, RVFI sequence,\n  or bus-stall behavior.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Separate true ID/EX holds for dmem and divide stalls from load-use and redirect bubble requests; retain load-use PC stalling and hold priority.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Capture ordinary payload fields during a bubble but clear valid, mem_read, mem_write, and reg_write; fully clear on reset and hold all fields on dmem or divide stalls.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Check dependent loads, redirects, and overlapping imem/dmem stalls for exact retirement order and absence of invalid-bubble memory or forwarding effects.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
