t hold. Do not forward a misaligned load\\nthat traps. Keep the existing EX/MEM priority for ordinary ALU results and\\nthe MEM/WB fallback for older writers. The bypass should reduce load-use\\nstalls while preserving RVFI operand values and exact memory semantics.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.\n…[77894 of 80966 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:02b7b7e4303aacd2]…\nre.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire prediction, training, and accepted-EX control while preserving the nret=1 RVFI and memory interfaces.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Check warm loops and exits, stale instruction immediates, illegal branches, target alignment, bus stalls, wrong-path side effects, and RVFI PC and order.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 216.46, \"delta_pct\": -44.8, \"vs_baseline\": -23.46, \"fmax_mhz\": 93.34, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4312127, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5857, \"ff\": 2315, \"seeds\": [91.35, 94.51, 93.34], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-23T17:36:10.709848Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 6, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-23 hyp-20260923-003-r6s2 (regression, -44.80%): Registering a backward-branch lookahead still leaves live instruction opcode and B-immediate checks ahead of the IF PC target mux, so prediction can lose FPGA fitness despite moving the predecessor lookup out of the fetch cycle.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
