{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n x=json.loads(l)\n if x['id'] in ('hyp-20260923-001-r5s0','hyp-20260923-001-r6s0','hyp-20260923-001-r7s0'):\n  print(x['id'],x.get('title'))\n  print('HYP:',x['hypothesis']['hypothesis'] if isinstance(x['hypothesis'],dict) else x['hypothesis'])\n  print('NUM:',x.get('fmax_mhz'),x.get('lut4'),x.get('cycles'))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"hyp-20260923-001-r5s0 Bank the register-file read muxes\nHYP: Keep the same 32 x 32 flip-flop register array and synchronous write port,\nbut implement each asynchronous read as four local eight-register banks.\nDecode the low three address bits once per read port into one-hot selects,\nOR the selected register within each bank, then select one of the four bank\nresults with the high two address bits. Keep x0 hardwired to zero and retain\nthe existing same-cycle WB write-through priority. This bounded local read\nnetwork should map to fewer serial LUT and routing levels on the measured\ninstruction-to-ID/EX operand path, improving median Fmax while preserving\nthe single-issue retirement stream and all RVFI values.\n\nNUM: 153.99 5569 4491817\nhyp-20260923-001-r6s0 Clear only side-effect controls on ID/EX bubbles\nHYP: Make load-use and redirect bubbles invalidate only the ID/EX valid bit and\nthe three controls that can affect memory or forwarding: mem_read,\nmem_write, and reg_write. Let the remaining payload capture its normal\ndecoded values on a bubble; those values cannot cause architectural\neffects while valid is zero and the side-effect controls are clear. Keep\nfull reset behavior. Give dmem and divide holds priority over a bubble,\nwhile retaining the existing PC hold on load-use. This removes the hazard\nresult from the wide ID/EX data-register reset/enable network and should\nimprove Fmax without changing the retirement cycle count, RVFI sequence,\nor bus-stall behavior.\n\nNUM: 183.52 5659 4491817\nhyp-20260923-001-r7s0 Remove reset muxes from ID/EX payload registers\nHYP: Split ID/EX storage so reset clears valid and the complete control word,\nwhile PC, instruction, register operands and addresses, immediate, destination,\nand one-hot ALU select flops have no reset input. Keep their normal capture\nand hold behavior, including the existing bubble rule that clears valid and\nmemory/writeback side-effect controls. An invalid ID/EX entry must still\nproduce no redirect, divide launch, memory request, register write, or\nretirement; the reset control word provides that guard until a real fetch is\ncaptured. This should remove a reset mux and high-fanout reset routing from\nthe wide decode destination without adding cycles or a new EX bypass path.\n\nNUM: 161.63 5641 4491817\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
