{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -c \"git diff --check && git status --short && sed -n '1,90p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260923-001-r9s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260923-001-r9s0\ntitle: \"Remove the invalid-fetch NOP mux from register-file reads\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  Prior routed analysis identified the live instruction-input to ID/EX\n  register-file read as a critical path. The current IF stage selects a NOP\n  ahead of every instruction bit when fetch is invalid or EX redirects, so\n  even the source-register addresses traverse that mux before the 32-entry\n  register-file read. Earlier register-file banking and EX retiming reduced\n  fitness; removing this existing input mux is a smaller change to that path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Pass the raw imem instruction through IF/ID every cycle and use IF/ID.valid\n  to mark unavailable or wrong-path fetches. In ID, continue to capture the\n  ordinary payload, but force valid, mem_read, mem_write, and reg_write low\n  for an invalid fetch or a flush. In the hazard unit, qualify load-use\n  detection with IF/ID.valid so arbitrary instruction bits during a redirect\n  or imem stall cannot hold the PC. EX already qualifies redirects and divide\n  launches with validity. This removes the flush/redirect NOP mux from the\n  instruction-to-register-file path without adding a stage, changing cycle\n  behavior, or allowing an invalid instruction to access memory or retire.\n  Keep decoder default-illegal behavior and all RVFI and bus-stall checks.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Drive IF/ID.instr from imem_data directly; retain the existing valid, PC stall, and redirect rules.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Gate the three side-effect controls as well as valid with IF/ID.valid and flush when ID/EX captures an invalid fetch.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Require a valid IF/ID instruction for load-use detection so wrong-path or unavailable raw instruction bits cannot cause false stalls.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect IF/ID.valid to the hazard unit without changing the nret=1 top-level interface.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Check redirects and imem stalls with raw words that alias a load destination, plus suppression of memory writes, register writes, and RVFI retirement for invalid fetches.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
