tream interlock only\\nwhen that result is accepted. Keep all RV32I operations and four MUL variants\\nsingle-cycle. Implement exact RV32M signed, unsigned, divide-by-zero, and\\nINT_MIN/-1 behavior. Preserve the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS result substitutions and\\nexercise the same launch/complete interlock in formal mode. This should raise\\nmedian Fmax with negligible ch\n…[38775 of 41847 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:48ad1e44b0f5c6d1]…\nload-use and redirect bubble semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Separate EX/MEM control reset from datapath updates, and make divider metadata usable only after its launch capture while preserving dmem-stall priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Reset MEM/WB validity and side-effect control only; retain prior payload and forwarding metadata during dmem stalls exactly as before.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Check reset release, bubbles, redirects, divide completion, and repeated dmem stalls for absence of stray writes or retirements and exact ordered RVFI data.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 311.86, \"delta_pct\": -23.67, \"vs_baseline\": 10.27, \"fmax_mhz\": 140.08, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491817, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5669, \"ff\": 2190, \"seeds\": [140.37, 137.08, 140.08], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-23T18:32:41.294036Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 9}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
