{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_2", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/zsh -c \"rg -n '\\\"category\\\": \\\"structural\\\"|category: structural|structural' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260923-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Decouple DIV and REM with an iterative EX unit\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The bench core puts four full-width combinational divide and remainder operations\\non its one-cycle EX datapath. That costs LUTs and can constrain Fmax for every\\nCoreMark instruction, while the timed matrix, list, and state loop has effectively\\nno divide traffic. A closely related reference core gained Fmax and shed thousands\\nof LUTs after moving these operations to a multicycle unit. The bench baseline has\\nonly 437 LUT4s of margin under its 10000-LUT4 target, making this structural change\\nespecially promising.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The bench core puts four full-width combinational divide and remainder operations\\non its one-cycle EX datapath. That costs LUTs and can constrain Fmax for every\\nCoreMark instruction, while the timed matrix, list, and state loop has effectively\\nno divide traffic. A closely related reference core gained Fmax and shed thousands\\nof LUTs after moving these operations to a multicycle unit. The bench baseline has\\nonly 437 LUT4s of margin under its 10000-LUT4 target, making this structural change\\nespecially promising.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the combinational DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU datapaths with one 32-step\\nrestoring divider attached to EX. On a divide-class instruction, capture the\\npost-forwarded operands and complete ID/EX metadata once, freeze younger fetch\\nand decode, and let older MEM/WB work drain through invalid EX/MEM bubbles.\\nWhen the divider finishes, advance exactly one EX/MEM result with the captured\\nmetadata; preserve dmem-stall priority and release the upstream interlock only\\nwhen t