{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260923-002-r13s1.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260923-002-r13s1\ntitle: \"Move the register file from resettable flops to distributed RAM\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  A routed timing path in the current bench core starts at a register-file\n  flop and traverses the asynchronous read network into ID/EX. The existing\n  32-by-32 resettable flop array makes both read ports wide routed muxes.\n  Earlier one-hot banking and mirrored flop arrays lost Fmax; the Gowin\n  synthesis flow has asynchronous-read distributed-RAM primitives that offer\n  a different storage structure without adding a pipeline stage or cycles.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the resettable flop array with two identical 32-by-32 inferred\n  distributed-RAM copies, one asynchronous read port per copy and the same\n  synchronous architectural write applied to both. Do not reset the RAM\n  contents. Instead, reset one valid bit per nonzero register; an unwritten\n  register reads as zero, and a committed write sets its valid bit. Preserve\n  x0, the current same-cycle write-first bypass, and the reg_file interface.\n  Keep the validity gate outside each memory's read expression so synthesis\n  can map the memories to Gowin LUTRAM. This should reduce the flop array's\n  read-routing and reset burden on the measured RF-to-ID/EX path, raising\n  Fmax while leaving CoreMark's issue, stall, and retirement cycles intact.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/reg_file.sv\n    description: \"Use two write-mirrored single-read distributed memories, a resettable per-register valid bitmap, x0 gating, and the existing write-first bypass semantics.\"\n  - file: test/test_reg_file.py\n    description: \"Check both read ports, same-cycle bypass, x0, writes followed by reset, and zero reads from stale uninitialized RAM entries.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
