{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/zsh -c \"rg -n 'critical|timing|path|RF-to|Fmax' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | tail -6\"", "aggregated_output": "35:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260923-001-r12s0\", \"title\": \"Segment the sequential PC incrementers\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The fetch PC and EX fall-through/link paths each compute a 32-bit PC+4.\\nTheir carry chains can constrain Fmax even though they add no useful work\\nto CoreMark. Segmenting the wider RVFI order incrementer previously raised\\nFmax, while attempts that added decoding or target selection to the PC path\\nlost timing. The existing PC+4 paths have not received the same local\\ncarry-path optimization.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The fetch PC and EX fall-through/link paths each compute a 32-bit PC+4.\\nTheir carry chains can constrain Fmax even though they add no useful work\\nto CoreMark. Segmenting the wider RVFI order incrementer previously raised\\nFmax, while attempts that added decoding or target selection to the PC path\\nlost timing. The existing PC+4 paths have not received the same local\\ncarry-path optimization.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace each PC+4 expression in IF and EX with four fixed-width increment\\nslices. Increment bits 9:2 unconditionally; increment each higher slice\\nonly when every lower PC bit from bit 2 is one, with those carry enables\\nformed in parallel. Pass bits 1:0 through unchanged, preserving exact\\nmodulo-2^32 addition by four for every PC value. Reuse the EX result for\\nboth the link value and fall-through RVFI next PC. Keep redirect targets,\\nstall priority, stage boundaries, and all other ALU arithmetic unchanged.\\nThis should shorten the ordinary PC update and EX PC+4 paths without a\\ncycle penalty or another mux on branch recovery.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", 