{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/zsh -c \"rg -n 'mul|multiply|iterations|cycles|istall' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | tail -10\"", "aggregated_output": "31:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260923-003-r10s2\", \"title\": \"Predict same-page backward branches with a short target adder\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"Repeated taken branches cost a fetch bubble in the current EX-resolved pipeline.\\nEarlier predictors saved roughly 4-6% of CoreMark cycles, but full-width\\ntarget selection, table lookup, or successor-PC comparison reduced Fmax more\\nthan the cycle savings helped. Backward loop branches offer a narrower case:\\ntheir direction can be predicted without a table, and a same-page target\\nneeds only a short addition in the fetch-to-PC path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Repeated taken branches cost a fetch bubble in the current EX-resolved pipeline.\\nEarlier predictors saved roughly 4-6% of CoreMark cycles, but full-width\\ntarget selection, table lookup, or successor-PC comparison reduced Fmax more\\nthan the cycle savings helped. Backward loop branches offer a narrower case:\\ntheir direction can be predicted without a table, and a same-page target\\nneeds only a short addition in the fetch-to-PC path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Statically predict taken only for a valid, legal backward conditional BRANCH\\nwhose target is aligned and remains within the current 4 KiB code page.\\nIn IF, form the signed B-immediate plus PC[11:0] with a 13-bit adder; require\\nno page underflow and a word-aligned result. On an accepted fetch, select\\nthe resulting low 12 target bits while retaining PC[31:12]. Other fetches\\nkeep the existing PC+4 path. Add no history table, target RAM, or full-width\\npredicted-versus-resolved PC comparison.\\n\\nCarry one predicted-taken bit with the instruction into EX. EX still resolves\\nthe real branch condition using forwarded operands and reports its exact\\narchitectural next PC in RVFI. Suppress the ordinary redirect for a correct\\nprediction; on an untaken prediction, redirect immediately to branch PC+4\\nand squash the fetched target instruction. Unpredicted taken branches use\\nthe existing target redirect. Permit prediction only when IF/ID advances;\\npreserve t\n…[40344 of 43416 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:aecc56c4fb6fb7b6]…\n, alignment, and immediate signature; suppress only correct redirects and repair all mismatches.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Connect EX training and prediction verification to fetch and hazard control without changing the single-retire interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Flush younger work on misprediction and qualify predictor updates with EX advancement through bus and divide holds.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Check repeated taken loops, untaken exits, table collisions, changed instructions, block boundaries, stalls, wrong-path effects, and RVFI PC and order.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 266.73, \"delta_pct\": -34.72, \"vs_baseline\": -5.69, \"fmax_mhz\": 114.93, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4308871, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5962, \"ff\": 2480, \"seeds\": [113.17, 114.93, 115.33], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-23T19:59:57.012965Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 13}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
