{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/zsh -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'] in ['hyp-20260923-001-r1s0','hyp-20260923-002-r9s1','hyp-20260923-002-r10s1','hyp-20260923-001-r5s0','hyp-20260923-001-r10s0']:\n  print('\\\\n',d['id'], d['title'], d['category'], d['fitness'],d['fmax_mhz'],d['cycles'],d['lut4'])\n  print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'] if isinstance(d['hypothesis'],dict) else d['hypothesis'])\n  print(d.get('implementation_notes','')[:1000])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\n hyp-20260923-001-r1s0 Forward live MEM load data into EX micro_opt 259.28 111.17 4287652 9951\nAdd a MEM-to-EX bypass for the current load's fully extracted and extended\ndata, and let the dependent instruction enter EX directly behind the load.\nWhen dmem is not ready, hold both instructions until the response is valid;\nsuppress EX redirects during that hold. Do not forward a misaligned load\nthat traps. Keep the existing EX/MEM priority for ordinary ALU results and\nthe MEM/WB fallback for older writers. The bypass should reduce load-use\nstalls while preserving RVFI operand values and exact memory semantics.\n\n\n\n hyp-20260923-001-r5s0 Bank the register-file read muxes micro_opt 342.82 153.99 4491817 5569\nKeep the same 32 x 32 flip-flop register array and synchronous write port,\nbut implement each asynchronous read as four local eight-register banks.\nDecode the low three address bits once per read port into one-hot selects,\nOR the selected register within each bank, then select one of the four bank\nresults with the high two address bits. Keep x0 hardwired to zero and retain\nthe existing same-cycle WB write-through priority. This bounded local read\nnetwork should map to fewer serial LUT and routing levels on the measured\ninstruction-to-ID/EX operand path, improving median Fmax while preserving\nthe single-issue retirement stream and all RVFI values.\n\n\n\n hyp-20260923-002-r9s1 Separate pipeline validity reset from datapath payload structural 311.86 140.08 4491817 5669\nSplit each pipeline register into a narrow resettable control sideband and\nan unreset datapath payload. On reset, clear valid plus every control bit\nthat can trigger a memory access, forwarding, divide launch, or register\nwrite. Let PC, instruction, operands, immediates, arithmetic results, and\nRVFI data fields update on their existing stage-accept enables without a\nreset mux. Keep the current hold and bubble priorities, including MEM/WB\npayload retention during dmem stalls and divider metadata capture before\ncompletion. An entry may use payload only after\n…[1066 of 4138 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:55c3e27cc94c022b]…\n routed Fmax.\n\n\n\n hyp-20260923-002-r10s1 Eliminate the divider's duplicate pipeline register structural 399.13 179.28 4491817 5545\nRemove the full-width div_meta_q register. At divider launch, retain only\nthe two post-forwarding source values needed for exact RVFI rs1/rs2 data;\nthe divider continues to capture its arithmetic operands as today. While\ndivision runs or its completed result waits for dmem backpressure, keep\nID/EX held. On the accepting edge, construct one EX/MEM divide entry from\nthe held ID/EX PC, instruction, addresses, destination and controls, the\nsaved source values, div_result, and PC+4. Set branch-only and unused store\nfields to zero. Let older work drain and emit invalid EX/MEM bubbles during\nthe wait, exactly as in the current interlock. This removes a wide duplicate\nstage register and its input logic without adding a CoreMark cycle or a mux\nto the ordinary fetch and ALU paths. Preserve the existing real and ALTOPS\ndivider behavior, ordered nret=1 retirement, and all stall priorities.\n\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
