{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260923-002-r14s1.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260923-002-r14s1\ntitle: \"Share the unsigned multiplier with a short high-half completion stage\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  EX still contains three separate 64-bit products for MULH, MULHU, and\n  MULHSU even though CoreMark's timed path uses low-half MUL and has no\n  high-half multiply instructions. Earlier sharing put signedness selection\n  before a wider multiplier and lost Fmax; the 32-step high-half unit also\n  added more control and registers than this rare operation warrants. A\n  single unsigned 32-by-32 product can serve all four instructions without\n  putting operand selection ahead of CoreMark's single-cycle MUL path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Keep the existing one-cycle low-half MUL result from an unsigned 32-by-32\n  product. Use that same product's high word for MULHU and as the basis for\n  signed high-half results. For MULH and MULHSU, form the correction in\n  parallel with the product: add b when a is negative, and additionally add\n  a when b is negative for MULH. Capture the unsigned high word, correction,\n  post-forwarded operands, and instruction metadata on a high-half launch;\n  finish with one 32-bit subtraction on the following cycle. MULHU uses a\n  zero correction. Emit one EX/MEM entry only when the result is accepted,\n  hold younger instructions while it completes, and let older work drain.\n  Reuse the existing multicycle EX metadata and stall discipline, including\n  dmem backpressure and one-time RVFI retirement. Keep DIV/REM and ordinary\n  integer operations unchanged. Under RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS, produce the exact\n  prescribed high-half substitutions through the same launch/completion\n  handshake. This removes two full products and keeps signedness logic off\n  the multiplier input and the timed low-half MUL path; the additional\n  high-half cycle should not change CoreMark's measured cycle count.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Expose the high word of one unsigned 32-by-32 product, retain single-cycle MUL, and remove the separate signed products while preserving ALTOPS outputs.\"\n  - file: rtl/mulh_unit.sv\n    description: \"Capture unsigned product high word and parallel signed correction, then subtract in a short completion stage with a stable result until consumed.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Launch high-half operations with forwarded operands, retain their RVFI metadata, and inject exactly one completed EX/MEM result through dmem stalls.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Extend the existing EX multicycle hold to the high-half completion cycle while preserving load-use, redirect, and bus-stall priorities.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect the combined EX hold to pipeline control without changing the nret=1 top-level ports or retirement order.\"\n  - file: test/test_mulh_unit.py\n    description: \"Check all three high-half operations against full RV32M products, including sign boundaries, randomized operands, held completion, and back-to-back launches.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Check high-half instruction interlocks, dependent forwarding, dmem stalls, and exactly once ordered RVFI retirement.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
