{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d.get('category')=='structural' and d['id'] in ['hyp-20260923-002-r9s1','hyp-20260923-002-r10s1','hyp-20260923-002-r12s1']:\n  print('\\\\n',d['id'],d['title'],'\\\\n',d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"\n hyp-20260923-002-r9s1 Separate pipeline validity reset from datapath payload \n Split each pipeline register into a narrow resettable control sideband and\nan unreset datapath payload. On reset, clear valid plus every control bit\nthat can trigger a memory access, forwarding, divide launch, or register\nwrite. Let PC, instruction, operands, immediates, arithmetic results, and\nRVFI data fields update on their existing stage-accept enables without a\nreset mux. Keep the current hold and bubble priorities, including MEM/WB\npayload retention during dmem stalls and divider metadata capture before\ncompletion. An entry may use payload only after its valid and side-effect\ncontrols establish that the payload was captured. Preserve the nret=1\ninterface, exact RVFI retirement values and order, traps, and all RV32IM\nresults. The expected gain is higher routed Fmax at the same instruction\ncount and CoreMark cycle count.\n\n\n hyp-20260923-002-r10s1 Eliminate the divider's duplicate pipeline register \n Remove the full-width div_meta_q register. At divider launch, retain only\nthe two post-forwarding source values needed for exact RVFI rs1/rs2 data;\nthe divider continues to capture its arithmetic operands as today. While\ndivision runs or its completed result waits for dmem backpressure, keep\nID/EX held. On the accepting edge, construct one EX/MEM divide entry from\nthe held ID/EX PC, instruction, addresses, destination and controls, the\nsaved source values, div_result, and PC+4. Set branch-only and unused store\nfields to zero. Let older work drain and emit invalid EX/MEM bubbles during\nthe wait, exactly as in the current interlock. This removes a wide duplicate\nstage register and its input logic without adding a CoreMark cycle or a mux\nto the ordinary fetch and ALU paths. Preserve the existing real and ALTOPS\ndivider behavior, ordered nret=1 retirement, and all stall priorities.\n\n\n hyp-20260923-002-r12s1 Register the final writeback value at the MEM/WB boundary \n Select the architectural destination value in MEM and register that single\n32-bit value at MEM/WB in place of the separate ALU-result and load-result\nregisters. Drive WB, EX forwarding, and RVFI rd_wdata directly from this\nregistered value. Keep the load extraction, memory access, trap controls,\nand all other RVFI fields unchanged. During dmem backpressure, retain the\nlast MEM/WB destination value and forwarding metadata while clearing only\nretirement validity, as the current pipeline does. This moves selection\naway from the WB-to-operand path, removes one 32-bit register bank, and\nshould raise Fmax without changing issue, stall, or retirement cycles.\nThe added selection on the MEM-to-MEM/WB path is the timing tradeoff to\nmeasure with routed Fmax.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
