{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260923-002-r15s1.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260923-002-r15s1\ntitle: \"Pipeline multiplication across EX and MEM\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current EX stage must finish three full-width products and select their\n  results in one clock, even though ordinary CoreMark instructions do not use\n  the high-half variants. Earlier high-half-only units added an EX interlock\n  without shortening the common low-half MUL path and lost Fmax. Splitting all\n  multiplication at the existing EX/MEM boundary targets that path while\n  allowing independent instructions to keep issuing every cycle.\nhypothesis: |\n  In EX, compute four unsigned 16-by-16 partial products from the forwarded\n  operands and register them with the instruction metadata in EX/MEM. Remove\n  MUL, MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU from the EX ALU result selection so no full\n  product feeds the EX/MEM register. In MEM, combine the registered partials\n  into the low or high 32-bit result, applying signed high-half corrections\n  from the registered source operands, and capture that result in MEM/WB.\n\n  Treat a MUL-family instruction in ID/EX like a load for an immediately\n  dependent successor: insert one bubble, then forward its completed MEM/WB\n  result. Do not forward the incomplete EX/MEM value. Independent successors\n  continue at one instruction per cycle. Preserve the existing divide\n  handshake, memory backpressure, traps, single-channel retirement, and exact\n  RV32M results. Under RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS, carry the prescribed substitute\n  result through the same EX/MEM-to-MEM/WB latency. The extra cycle for a\n  dependent multiply should cost less than the Fmax gain from replacing a\n  full-width EX multiplier with registered 16-bit partial products.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/mul_partial.sv\n    description: \"Compute four 16-by-16 unsigned partial products from forwarded operands, with exact ALTOPS substitutes under the formal define.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Carry partial products and MUL-family operation metadata in EX/MEM without changing the nret=1 interface.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Register multiply partials with EX/MEM metadata and remove MUL-family results from the one-cycle ALU selection while preserving the divider path.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Assemble low and signed or unsigned high products from registered partials and capture the selected result in MEM/WB.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Give immediately dependent MUL successors the same single bubble as load-use hazards, retaining current bus and divide hold priorities.\"\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: \"Disallow EX/MEM forwarding for incomplete MUL results and forward their completed MEM/WB values.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire multiply readiness into hazard and forwarding controls without changing top-level ports or retirement order.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Check all MUL-family results and RVFI fields, dependent and independent successors, and overlapping instruction and data bus stalls without reducing existing ALU vector coverage.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
