{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -c \"rg -n 'liveness|depth|ALTOPS|unique|cover' formal/checks_si.cfg formal/run_all.sh | head -100\"","aggregated_output":"formal/run_all.sh:11:#   default: formal/checks.cfg       (fast, ALTOPS, used by orchestrator)\nformal/run_all.sh:12:#   deep   : formal/checks-deep.cfg  (no ALTOPS, proves M-ext arithmetic)\nformal/run_all.sh:190:        # branch never matches and the regular DONE (PASS branch covers it.\nformal/checks_si.cfg:6:[depth]\nformal/checks_si.cfg:7:# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\nformal/checks_si.cfg:8:# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\nformal/checks_si.cfg:15:# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\nformal/checks_si.cfg:16:# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\nformal/checks_si.cfg:18:# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nformal/checks_si.cfg:19:unique     1 10 20\nformal/checks_si.cfg:20:cover      1    20\nformal/checks_si.cfg:22:liveness   1 10 20\nformal/checks_si.cfg:26:# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Same as checks.cfg. See checks.cfg for\nformal/checks_si.cfg:27:# the full rationale on what ALTOPS does and does not prove. M-extension\nformal/checks_si.cfg:28:# arithmetic correctness is covered by test/test_alu.py and `make formal-deep`.\nformal/checks_si.cfg:29:`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\nformal/checks_si.cfg:31:[cover]\nformal/checks_si.cfg:32:# Sanity cover: the CPU must retire at least one non-trapping instruction.\nformal/checks_si.cfg:33:always @* if (!reset) cover (rvfi_valid && !rvfi_trap);\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
