{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260923-002-r2s1.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260923-002-r2s1\ntitle: \"Move high-half multiply off the single-cycle EX path\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The divider change raised fitness by removing rarely used wide arithmetic\n  from the one-cycle EX path. The ALU still builds three full 64-bit products\n  for MUL, MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU. Those high-half product paths must meet\n  the clock period even when CoreMark is executing ordinary 32-bit operations.\n  CoreMark's matrix arithmetic needs the low-half MUL throughput, so that\n  operation should remain single-cycle.\nhypothesis: |\n  Keep MUL as a single-cycle 32-bit low-product operation. Move MULH, MULHU,\n  and MULHSU into one shared iterative high-half multiplier attached to EX,\n  removing their wide combinational products from the ALU. Form the unsigned\n  64-bit product with a 32-step shift-add engine using a roughly 33-bit adder;\n  correct its high word for signed operands in separate completion cycles.\n  Capture forwarded operands and RVFI metadata once, hold younger instructions\n  while a high-half multiply runs, let older instructions drain, and present\n  one completed EX/MEM result only when the boundary accepts it. Keep the\n  result stable through dmem backpressure. Under RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS, use the\n  exact prescribed stand-in result with a short but real start/complete\n  handshake so the existing liveness depth remains meaningful. This should\n  shorten the EX critical path while preserving low-half MUL throughput and\n  ordered single-channel retirement.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Retain a 32-bit low-product MUL path; remove synthesized full-width high-half products while preserving ALTOPS mappings.\"\n  - file: rtl/mulh_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add a shared iterative high-half multiplier for MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU with signed correction, stable completion, and ALTOPS behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Route high-half operations through the new unit, capture forwarded operands and instruction metadata once, and release exactly one result after completion and dmem acceptance.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Extend the existing divide interlock to hold IF and ID for high-half multiply without blocking older retirement or losing redirect and bus-stall priority.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the combined multicycle EX hold into hazard control without changing the nret=1 port contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Keep the low-half MUL vectors and move existing high-half arithmetic vectors to the new unit test without reducing coverage.\"\n  - file: test/test_mulh_unit.py\n    description: \"Check signed and unsigned high halves, zero and INT_MIN cases, randomized products, back-to-back launches, and held completion.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Include the new RTL source and check high-half multiply followed by dependent instructions, exact RVFI data and order, and bus-stall interlocks.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
