{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260923-002-r3s1.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260923-002-r3s1\ntitle: \"Decouple fetch from issue with a two-entry prefetch queue\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current IF stage holds its fetch PC whenever load-use, dmem, or divider\n  backpressure stops decode. It discards otherwise ready instruction-bus cycles\n  during those pauses, then pays a fresh imem stall when issue resumes. The\n  fitness cosim independently rejects about 22% of instruction fetch cycles.\n  A small elastic queue can use paused issue cycles to fetch ahead without\n  adding a predictor or lengthening the zero-wait pipeline.\nhypothesis: |\n  Give IF a two-entry FIFO of {PC, instruction} pairs and a separate fetch PC.\n  Fetch into free FIFO space whenever io_imemReady is high, including cycles\n  when ID is held by load-use, dmem, or division. Issue the FIFO head when\n  available; when empty, bypass a ready imem word directly into the existing\n  ID/EX register, preserving the present zero-wait latency. An empty FIFO and\n  an unready bus produce the existing bubble. Allow simultaneous dequeue and\n  enqueue, and advance the fetch PC only for accepted words. On an EX redirect,\n  discard all queued wrong-path words, suppress same-cycle wrong-path issue,\n  and restart fetching at the resolved target with redirect priority over\n  both bus and pipeline stalls. Keep each instruction's PC paired with its\n  word for RVFI, and retain the nret=1 retirement interface and all existing\n  trap and memory semantics. This should recover part of the imem-stall cost\n  with only a small fetch-side register and mux footprint, leaving the EX\n  arithmetic critical path untouched.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add the two-entry PC/instruction FIFO, empty-queue bypass, independent fetch cursor, simultaneous push/pop handling, and redirect flush.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Stall issue only when no queued or live instruction is available; let fetch fill the FIFO while ID is held, preserving load-use and dmem priorities.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire instruction availability and issue backpressure between IF and the hazard unit without changing top-level bus or RVFI ports.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Exercise queue fill and drain under imem/dmem stalls, load-use and divider holds, redirect flushes, and exact once-only ordered RVFI retirement.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
