{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -c \"git status --short && sed -n '1,120p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260923-002-r4s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260923-002-r4s1\ntitle: \"Retire stalled RAM stores through a one-entry slot\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  A store in MEM currently freezes the entire pipeline whenever dmem is not\n  ready, although its address, data, and byte mask are already known. The\n  fitness run applies random dmem stalls, so those freezes cost CoreMark\n  cycles. A one-entry pending-store slot improved fitness in the read-only\n  v1 reference, while the bench experiments show that adding fetch-path\n  selection or a live load-to-EX bypass can lose more Fmax than it saves in\n  cycles. The bench core has ample LUT margin after its iterative divider.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add one pending-store slot for valid, aligned stores in normal RAM below\n  0x00100000. When such a store reaches MEM with an empty slot and dmem is\n  ready, keep the present direct write path. When dmem is not ready, capture\n  its byte address, replicated write data, and byte mask in the slot, advance\n  it once into MEM/WB with its original RVFI memory fields, and let younger\n  non-memory instructions progress. The slot owns the dmem port until its\n  write handshakes; younger loads and stores wait behind it to preserve\n  memory order. MMIO, UART, and timing-marker stores always wait for the\n  direct bus handshake, and trapping or misaligned accesses never enqueue.\n  Preserve the existing full-pipeline hold for a blocked load or a memory\n  operation waiting behind the slot. This should hide some store-only dmem\n  stalls without adding a path through fetch, EX operands, or load data.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/store_slot.sv\n    description: \"Add a one-entry register holding the pending RAM store address, replicated data, byte mask, and valid bit until one ready-cycle drain.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Classify bufferable aligned RAM stores, enqueue only on an unready direct port, preserve their MEM/WB and RVFI fields on enqueue, and expose precise memory backpressure.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Use precise MEM backpressure so only blocked loads, nonbufferable stores, or operations behind the occupied slot freeze the pipeline.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Instantiate the slot and give a pending store priority at the dmem port, retaining the nret=1 top-level ports and channel-0 retirement order.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Exercise stalled RAM-store enqueue and drain, subsequent ALU progress, load/store ordering, MMIO marker handshakes, misaligned traps, random bus stalls, and exact once-only RVFI retirement.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
