edirects during that hold. Do not forward a misaligned load\\nthat traps. Keep the existing EX/MEM priority for ordinary ALU results and\\nthe MEM/WB fallback for older writers. The bypass should reduce load-use\\nstalls while preserving RVFI operand values and exact memory semantics.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.\n…[51948 of 55020 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:09f8d07e5c1f5278]…\n, \"description\": \"Flush younger work on misprediction and defer recovery and training while EX is blocked by a data-memory stall or divide hold.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Check repeated loop branches, loop exits, stale or changed instructions, misaligned targets, bus stalls, wrong-path suppression, and RVFI PC and order correctness.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 189.79, \"delta_pct\": -47.56, \"vs_baseline\": -32.89, \"fmax_mhz\": 81.84, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4312067, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5866, \"ff\": 2260, \"seeds\": [82.39, 81.84, 77.77], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-23T16:50:12.050067Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 4, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-23 hyp-20260923-003-r4s2 (regression, -47.56%): Even a one-entry backward-loop predictor can lose fitness when full-width predicted/resolved PC comparison extends EX-to-IF recovery: Fmax fell to 81.8 MHz, overwhelming the modest CoreMark cycle saving.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
