{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/zsh -c \"rg -n 'critical path|5\\\\.66|IF/ID|fetch register|pipeline stage|stage boundary' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl cores/bench/LESSONS.md\"", "aggregated_output": "cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:4:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260923-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Predict control flow with a small branch target buffer\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current fetch PC advances by four until EX resolves every taken branch or jump. Each taken control transfer flushes the younger instruction, wasting a cycle in a branch-heavy CoreMark loop. A small predictor can remove that bubble on repeated control transfers without changing retirement or the memory interface.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current fetch PC advances by four until EX resolves every taken branch or jump. Each taken control transfer flushes the younger instruction, wasting a cycle in a branch-heavy CoreMark loop. A small predictor can remove that bubble on repeated control transfers without changing retirement or the memory interface.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a 16-entry direct-mapped, fully tagged branch target buffer at fetch. Each entry holds a target and a two-bit saturating direction counter; unconditional JAL/JALR entries always predict taken. On a tag miss, fetch proceeds sequentially. Train only when a valid control-flow instruction advances through EX, using its resolved aligned target and outcome. Carry the exact predicted next PC with the instruction into EX, and redirect/flush younger work only when it differs from the resolved next PC. Suppress training and recovery while EX is held by a dmem stall, then perform them when EX advances. Preserve the existing sequential next PC and trap behavior for misaligned targets, and correct stale predictions even if the instruction at a trained PC changes. This should save cycles on recurring CoreMark branches and calls while keeping the added lookup small enough to limit Fmax loss.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the tagged 16-entry target/direction table, predict the fetch successor PC, and give EX recovery priority over fetch stalls. Reset entry valid bits and updat\n…[38629 of 41701 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:88b68032c52c4eeb]…\nuash wrong-path EX work while recovery is pending.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Connect predictor training, successor metadata, recovery, and EX kill control without changing the nret=1 top-level ports.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Flush younger work on registered recovery, preserve redirect priority over imem and dmem stalls, and prevent wrong-path issue or retirement.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Check warmed branches and jumps, loop exits, JALR target changes, stale entries, collisions, misaligned targets, bus stalls, wrong-path side effects, and RVFI PCs and order.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 322.28, \"delta_pct\": -17.82, \"vs_baseline\": 13.95, \"fmax_mhz\": 139.76, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4336654, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 8111, \"ff\": 3270, \"seeds\": [138.2, 139.76, 142.09], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-23T17:17:15.780193Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 5}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
