{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260923-002-r6s1.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260923-002-r6s1\ntitle: \"Register fetch before decode and register-file read\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current IF/ID bundle is combinational, so a fetched instruction passes\n  through instruction memory and a 32-register source read before reaching\n  the ID/EX flip-flops. A routed critical path was measured from the\n  instruction input through that register-file read at 5.66 ns. The earlier\n  two-entry prefetch queue reduced CoreMark cycles but lost Fmax through its\n  FIFO-head/live-bus bypass and control. A single pipeline register can cut\n  the measured path without placing queue selection on the decode input.\nhypothesis: |\n  Turn IF/ID into one registered {PC, instruction, valid} stage and use its\n  output exclusively for decode, register-file read, and load-use detection.\n  Fetch captures a word only when io_imemReady is high; otherwise it holds\n  the fetch PC and inserts an invalid IF/ID bubble after the previous word\n  has been consumed. Hold both the fetch PC and IF/ID payload when ID cannot\n  advance because of load-use, division, or a data-memory stall. On an EX\n  redirect, invalidate IF/ID and flush ID/EX together, with the redirect PC\n  taking priority over all bus stalls. Keep EX, MEM, WB, nret=1 RVFI, and\n  architectural results unchanged. This adds one bubble for taken control\n  transfers, but should raise median Fmax enough to more than offset that\n  cycle cost by removing the instruction-memory-to-register-file timing path.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Register the IF/ID PC, instruction, and valid bit; advance fetch only on an accepted imem word, preserve buffered work under downstream stalls, and invalidate it on EX redirect.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Separate a missing imem response from downstream stalls so a buffered IF/ID instruction can drain exactly once; preserve load-use, divide, dmem, and redirect priorities.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the registered fetch stage and its consume/hold controls into decode and hazard detection while preserving the single-channel RVFI interface.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Check instruction and PC order across ready toggles, load-use and divide holds, data-memory stalls, taken redirects, and wrong-path suppression.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
