{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -c 'cat schemas/hypothesis.schema.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\"id\",\"title\",\"category\",\"motivation\",\"hypothesis\",\"expected_impact\",\"changes\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\":       {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^hyp-[0-9]{8}-[0-9]{3}(-r[0-9]+s[0-9]+)?$\"},\n    \"title\":    {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\.py)$\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/zsh -c \"rg -n \\\"critical path|timing path|fmax|multiplier|branch\\\" cores/bench/experiments -g '*.md' -g '*.json' -g '*.jsonl' | tail -30\"", "aggregated_output": "cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:1:{\"id\": \"baseline-bench-693038e\", \"title\": \"Baseline retest for cores/bench\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 282.82, \"delta_pct\": 0.0, \"vs_baseline\": 0.0, \"fmax_mhz\": 127.03, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 9563, \"ff\": 1866, \"seeds\": [128.72, 127.03, 123.02], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-23T15:32:48.790916Z\", \"round_id\": 0, \"slot\": 0}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260923-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Forward live MEM load data into EX\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The in-order pipeline inserts a bubble whenever an instruction immediately\\nconsumes a load result, even though the zero-wait memory model presents that\\nresult combinationally while the load is in MEM. CoreMark's list and matrix\\ncode repeatedly loads a value before using it. Removing these bubbles should\\nimprove iterations per cycle without changing the retirement width.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The in-order pipeline inserts a bubble whenever an instruction immediately\\nconsumes a load result, even though the zero-wait memory model presents that\\nresult combinationally while the load is in MEM. CoreMark's list and matrix\\ncode repeatedly loads a value before using it. Removing these bubbles should\\nimprove iterations per cycle without changing the retirement width.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a MEM-to-EX bypass for the current load's fully extracted and extended\\ndata, and let the dependent instruction enter EX directly behind the load.\\nWhen dmem is not ready, hold both instructions until the response is valid;\\nsuppress EX redirects during that hold. Do not forward a misaligned load\\nthat traps. Keep the existing EX/MEM priority for ordinary ALU results and\\nthe MEM/WB fallback for older writers. The bypass should reduce load-use\\nstalls while preserving RVFI operand values and exact memory semantics.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pc\n…[78611 of 81683 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:2a4cde99a84d30fd]…\nrol while preserving the nret=1 RVFI and memory interfaces.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Check warm loops and exits, stale instruction immediates, illegal branches, target alignment, bus stalls, wrong-path side effects, and RVFI PC and order.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 216.46, \"delta_pct\": -44.8, \"vs_baseline\": -23.46, \"fmax_mhz\": 93.34, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4312127, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5857, \"ff\": 2315, \"seeds\": [91.35, 94.51, 93.34], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-23T17:36:10.709848Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 6, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-23 hyp-20260923-003-r6s2 (regression, -44.80%): Registering a backward-branch lookahead still leaves live instruction opcode and B-immediate checks ahead of the IF PC target mux, so prediction can lose FPGA fitness despite moving the predecessor lookup out of the fetch cycle.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/run_summary.json:14:  \"best_fmax_mhz\": 183.52,\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
