{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_3", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/zsh -c \"rg -n '\\\"category\\\": \\\"structural\\\"|structural|hyp-20260923-002-r9s1' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses schemas/hypothesis.schema.json\"", "aggregated_output": "schemas/hypothesis.schema.json:8:    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260923-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Decouple DIV and REM with an iterative EX unit\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The bench core puts four full-width combinational divide and remainder operations\\non its one-cycle EX datapath. That costs LUTs and can constrain Fmax for every\\nCoreMark instruction, while the timed matrix, list, and state loop has effectively\\nno divide traffic. A closely related reference core gained Fmax and shed thousands\\nof LUTs after moving these operations to a multicycle unit. The bench baseline has\\nonly 437 LUT4s of margin under its 10000-LUT4 target, making this structural change\\nespecially promising.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The bench core puts four full-width combinational divide and remainder operations\\non its one-cycle EX datapath. That costs LUTs and can constrain Fmax for every\\nCoreMark instruction, while the timed matrix, list, and state loop has effectively\\nno divide traffic. A closely related reference core gained Fmax and shed thousands\\nof LUTs after moving these operations to a multicycle unit. The bench baseline has\\nonly 437 LUT4s of margin under its 10000-LUT4 target, making this structural change\\nespecially promising.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the combinational DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU datapaths with one 32-step\\nrestoring divider attached to EX. On a divide-class instruction, capture the\\npost-forwarded operands and complete ID/EX metadata once, freeze younger fetch\\nand decode, and let older MEM/WB work drain through invalid EX/MEM bubbles.\\nWhen the divider finishes, advance exactly one EX/MEM result with the captured\\nmetadata; preserve dmem-stall priority and release the upstream interlock only\\nwhen that result is accepted. Keep all RV32I operations and four MUL variants\\nsingle-cycle. Implement exact RV32M signed, unsigned, divide-by-zero, and\\nINT_MIN/-1 behavi\n…[35020 of 38092 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:cc5639d4ef2e5e0d]…\n\", \"description\": \"Document the opcode-dependent meaning of the ID/EX immediate field without changing its width or the top-level interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Cover forward and backward branches, JAL, forwarded JALR, misaligned control targets, and redirects concurrent with imem or dmem stalls; check exact RVFI PC and retirement order.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 395.63, \"delta_pct\": -3.17, \"vs_baseline\": 39.89, \"fmax_mhz\": 177.71, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491817, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5707, \"ff\": 2216, \"seeds\": [182.08, 177.71, 170.21], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-23T18:11:13.632323Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 8, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-23 hyp-20260923-002-r8s1 (regression, -3.17%): Precomputing BRANCH/JAL targets in ID adds a PC-plus-immediate adder and opcode-gated mux before ID/EX; with CoreMark cycles unchanged, the lower Fmax outweighed the shorter EX redirect path.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
