{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260923-003-r12s2.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260923-003-r12s2\ntitle: \"Predict backward branches within a 256-byte block\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Taken branches still waste a fetch slot, but previous predictors lost more\n  Fmax than their cycle savings recovered. The closest attempt predicted\n  same-page backward branches and reduced CoreMark cycles by about 4%, yet\n  its 13-bit target calculation and 12-bit PC selection lowered Fmax enough\n  to regress by 1.79%. In the supplied CoreMark ELF, 80 of 134 static\n  backward conditional branches target the same 256-byte block, suggesting\n  that a narrower predictor can retain useful coverage.\nhypothesis: |\n  Predict taken only for a valid, legal conditional BRANCH with a negative\n  displacement whose aligned target stays in the current 256-byte block.\n  Detect that the B immediate fits a signed 8-bit displacement, add only\n  PC[7:0] and that displacement with a 9-bit result, and reject a borrow\n  out of the block. Update only the low eight PC bits on an accepted fetch;\n  retain PC[31:8] directly. Do not add a history table, target RAM, or\n  full-width predicted-versus-resolved PC comparison.\n\n  Carry one predicted-taken bit with the branch through ID/EX. EX continues\n  to use forwarded operands for the real condition and reports the exact\n  architectural next PC through RVFI. A correct prediction suppresses the\n  usual redirect; an untaken or trapping prediction redirects to the\n  branch fall-through and squashes younger work. Unpredicted taken branches\n  use the existing EX redirect. Older EX recovery has priority over a new\n  prediction, and prediction occurs only when fetch advances through imem,\n  load-use, divide, and dmem interlocks. The shorter adder and narrower PC\n  selection should recover enough Fmax to outweigh reduced branch coverage.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 2\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Recognize eligible backward branches, compute a 9-bit block-local target, and steer only the low eight PC bits on an accepted prediction.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add one predicted-taken bit to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch the prediction with its instruction and clear it for invalid or flushed entries while preserving it during holds.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Suppress correct predicted redirects and recover to fall-through on wrong predictions or traps, preserving RVFI next PC and side-effect rules.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect prediction and recovery to existing fetch and hazard controls without changing the nret=1 interface.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Check taken loops, untaken exits, block boundaries, misaligned targets, illegal branch encodings, bus stalls, wrong-path side effects, and RVFI PCs and order.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
