s 4336654 lut 8111\n   \nhyp-20260923-003-r6s2 Predict one hot backward branch with registered lookahead fitness 216.46 delta -44.8 fmax 93.34 cycles 4312127 lut 5857\n   - 2026-09-23 hyp-20260923-003-r6s2 (regression, -44.80%): Registering a backward-branch lookahead still leaves live instruction opcode and B-immediate checks ahead of the IF PC target mux, so prediction can lose FPGA fitness despite moving the predecessor lookup out of the fetch cycle.\nhyp-20260923-003-r7s2 Predict one hot loop with registered target and selective repair fitness 370.03 delta -9.43 fmax 160.08 cycles 4326193 lut 5824\n   - 2026-09-23 hyp-20260923-003-r7s2 (regression, -9.43%): Registering a one-entry loop target and delaying misprediction repair removes live IF checks, but the added IF PC selection and predicted-taken gating on the same-cycle EX redirect can still cost more timing than the hot-loop fetch cycles saved on CoreMark.\nhyp-20260923-003-r8s2 Replay a cached branch-target instruction fitness 252.03 delta -38.31 fmax 107.4 cycles 4261396 lut 5809\n   - 2026-09-23 hyp-20260923-003-r8s2 (regression, -38.31%): Even replay after a resolved branch can lose fitness when EX-qualified cached-instruction and successor muxes feed IF/ID in the same cycle; roughly 5% fewer CoreMark cycles could not offset Fmax falling from 183.52 to 107.4 MHz.\nhyp-20260923-003-r9s2 Predict branch direction at execute to shorten PC steering fitness 380.17 delta -6.95 fmax 174.92 cycles 4601157 lut 5806\n   - 2026-09-23 hyp-20260923-003-r9s2 (regression, -6.95%): Predicting branch direction only in EX retains the taken-branch redirect bubble on correct guesses while mispredictions add a registered repair cycle, so a direction table needs enough PC-path timing gain to offset its cycle cost.\nhyp-20260923-003-r10s2 Predict same-page backward branches with a short target adder fitness 401.26 delta -1.79 fmax 172.92 cycles 4309463 lut 5738\n   \nhyp-20260923-003-r11s2 Predict short direct jumps at fetch fitness 330.62 delta -19.08 fmax 146.93 cycles 4444081 lut 5688\n   \nhyp-20260923-003-r12s2 Predict backward branches within a 256-byte block fitness 398.68 delta -2.42 fmax 171.59 cycles 4303997 lut 5710\n   - 2026-09-23 hyp-20260923-003-r12s2 (regression, -2.42%): Reducing backward-branch target arithmetic to nine bits and PC selection to eight bits still leaves live branch decode, offset and boundary checks, and target selection on the fetch-PC path, so saved CoreMark fetch slots did not recover enough Fmax.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
