{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nids={'hyp-20260923-003-r5s2','hyp-20260923-003-r7s2','hyp-20260923-003-r8s2','hyp-20260923-003-r10s2','hyp-20260923-003-r2s2'}\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'] in ids:\n  print('\\\\nID',d['id'],'\\\\nTITLE',d['title'],'\\\\nHYPOTHESIS\\\\n',d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'] if isinstance(d['hypothesis'],dict) else d['hypothesis'],'\\\\nNOTES',d.get('implementation_notes','')[:4000])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/zsh -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nids={'hyp-20260923-003-r5s2','hyp-20260923-003-r7s2','hyp-20260923-003-r8s2','hyp-20260923-003-r10s2','hyp-20260923-003-r2s2'}\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'] in ids:\n  print('\\\\nID',d['id'],'\\\\nTITLE',d['title'],'\\\\nHYPOTHESIS\\\\n',d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'] if isinstance(d['hypothesis'],dict) else d['hypothesis'],'\\\\nNOTES',d.get('implementation_notes','')[:4000])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\nID hyp-20260923-003-r2s2 \nTITLE Add a tagged branch target buffer to the iterative-divider core \nHYPOTHESIS\n Add the previously validated 16-entry direct-mapped, fully tagged branch\ntarget buffer to the current iterative-divider pipeline. Store a target\nand two-bit direction counter per entry; predict trained conditional\nbranches from the counter and JAL/JALR as taken. On a miss, fetch PC+4.\nCarry the predicted successor PC with each instruction and compare it\nagainst the resolved successor in EX. Redirect and flush younger work\nonly on a mismatch, including stale entries for non-control instructions.\nTrain or invalidate only when EX advances, so dmem stalls cannot duplicate\nupdates or lose recovery. Preserve sequential trap behavior for misaligned\ntargets. The divider's LUT reduction should let the measured BTB cycle\ngain improve fitness without exceeding the area limit.\n \nNOTES \n\nID hyp-20260923-003-r5s2 \nTITLE Look ahead one fetch for branch target prediction \nHYPOTHESIS\n Add a 16-entry, fully tagged branch target buffer with two-bit direction\ncounters. During each ordinary fetch, look up PC+4 and register the hit,\ndirection, and target for the following sequential fetch. The current\nfetch selects between PC+4 and this registered target, so table selection\nand tag comparison are outside its same-cycle PC update path. Hold the\nlookahead record when fetch stalls, and invalidate it after a predicted\ntarget or an EX recovery; those nonsequential fetches proceed without a\nprediction until sequential lookahead is ready again. Train once when a\nvalid branch or jump advances from EX, and invalidate an entry when its\nmatching PC executes a non-control instruction.\n\nCarry the selected successor PC with the instruction. In EX, compare it\nagainst the resolved successor, including misaligned-target traps and\nchanging JALR targets, but register the recovery flag and target instead\nof feeding the comparison directly into the IF PC mux. On the following\ncycle, give registered recovery priority over bus stalls and squash the\n\n…[3626 of 6698 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:699f5421f7176b34]…\npage underflow and a word-aligned result. On an accepted fetch, select\nthe resulting low 12 target bits while retaining PC[31:12]. Other fetches\nkeep the existing PC+4 path. Add no history table, target RAM, or full-width\npredicted-versus-resolved PC comparison.\n\nCarry one predicted-taken bit with the instruction into EX. EX still resolves\nthe real branch condition using forwarded operands and reports its exact\narchitectural next PC in RVFI. Suppress the ordinary redirect for a correct\nprediction; on an untaken prediction, redirect immediately to branch PC+4\nand squash the fetched target instruction. Unpredicted taken branches use\nthe existing target redirect. Permit prediction only when IF/ID advances;\npreserve the bit across stalls and give older EX recovery priority. Leave\nmisaligned targets and illegal branch encodings on their existing trap paths.\nThis should recover hot-loop fetch cycles with substantially less PC-path\nlogic than the prior predictor attempts, though Fmax remains the main risk.\n \nNOTES \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
