{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260923-003-r1s2.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260923-003-r1s2\ntitle: \"Predict control flow with a small branch target buffer\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The current fetch PC advances by four until EX resolves every taken branch or jump. Each taken control transfer flushes the younger instruction, wasting a cycle in a branch-heavy CoreMark loop. A small predictor can remove that bubble on repeated control transfers without changing retirement or the memory interface.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a 16-entry direct-mapped, fully tagged branch target buffer at fetch. Each entry holds a target and a two-bit saturating direction counter; unconditional JAL/JALR entries always predict taken. On a tag miss, fetch proceeds sequentially. Train only when a valid control-flow instruction advances through EX, using its resolved aligned target and outcome. Carry the exact predicted next PC with the instruction into EX, and redirect/flush younger work only when it differs from the resolved next PC. Suppress training and recovery while EX is held by a dmem stall, then perform them when EX advances. Preserve the existing sequential next PC and trap behavior for misaligned targets, and correct stale predictions even if the instruction at a trained PC changes. This should save cycles on recurring CoreMark branches and calls while keeping the added lookup small enough to limit Fmax loss.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add the tagged 16-entry target/direction table, predict the fetch successor PC, and give EX recovery priority over fetch stalls. Reset entry valid bits and update entries only for accepted EX results.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Carry the predicted successor PC through the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch the predicted successor PC with the instruction when decode advances.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare predicted and resolved successor PCs, redirect only on a valid misprediction, and report committed branch or jump outcomes for predictor training.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect predictor lookup, EX training, misprediction recovery, and the existing stall signals.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Flush younger instructions only on misprediction and defer recovery while EX is held by a dmem stall.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Exercise repeated taken and untaken branches, JAL and changing JALR targets, wrong-path suppression, and recovery with instruction and data bus stalls; check RVFI order and PCs.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
