{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260923-003-r3s2.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260923-003-r3s2\ntitle: \"Predict direct branches with a direction-only history table\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The previous 16-entry target buffer reduced CoreMark from 4,491,817 to\n  4,234,021 timed cycles, but on the iterative-divider core it lowered Fmax\n  from 156.91 to 142.61 MHz and reduced fitness to 336.82. Direct branch and\n  JAL targets are encoded in the fetched instruction, so storing 32-bit\n  targets and comparing tags adds hardware that these transfers do not need.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the target-buffer approach with a 32-entry, untagged table of\n  two-bit saturating direction counters, indexed by fetch PC[6:2]. Initialize\n  counters weakly not taken. In IF, recognize only legal conditional BRANCH\n  encodings and JAL; predict a BRANCH from its counter, predict JAL taken,\n  and leave JALR sequential. Form a predicted taken target directly from the\n  fetched B/J immediate and PC. Carry only one predicted-taken bit through\n  ID/EX. In EX, compare that bit with the resolved control-flow outcome,\n  treating a misaligned target trap as sequential, and redirect to the\n  resolved next PC only on a mismatch. Train counters once per accepted,\n  valid conditional branch; suppress both training and recovery while EX is\n  held by a data-memory stall or divider. This should retain much of the\n  measured branch-cycle saving with a small table, no target RAM or tag\n  comparators, and no 32-bit predicted-PC pipeline register.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add the 32-entry direction table, legal direct-control predecode, B/J immediate target calculation, prediction-driven PC selection, and accepted-EX counter updates; keep recovery above fetch stalls.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a single predicted-taken bit to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles without changing the RVFI-facing payloads.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch the prediction bit only with an accepted valid fetched instruction.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Resolve the actual taken outcome including misalignment traps, recover on a direction mismatch, and expose a valid branch outcome for one-time table training only when EX advances.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire branch training, EX acceptance, and misprediction recovery to fetch while preserving the nret=1 top-level interface.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Check warmed taken and untaken branches, direct jumps, JALR fallback, aliased counters, illegal branch encodings, misaligned targets, bus stalls, and RVFI PC/order correctness.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
