{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260923-003-r4s2.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260923-003-r4s2\ntitle: \"Predict hot backward loops with one target register\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The 16-entry target buffer and 32-entry direction table each saved about 6%\n  of CoreMark cycles, but their fetch lookup paths reduced Fmax enough to lose\n  fitness. CoreMark loop branches are a useful narrower target: a repeated\n  backward branch has a stable destination and is usually taken until its exit.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add one fully tagged loop-target entry containing a valid bit, the branch PC,\n  and its resolved 32-bit target. Train it only when a valid, aligned, taken\n  backward conditional branch advances from EX; do not let jumps or forward\n  branches replace the entry. In IF, predict the stored target on an exact PC\n  match and otherwise use PC+4. This removes fetched-instruction predecode,\n  direction-table lookup, and an IF target adder from the earlier predictor's\n  timing path. Carry the exact predicted successor PC into EX and redirect only\n  when it differs from the resolved successor, including loop exit, stale code,\n  and misaligned-target cases. Invalidate a stale entry when its matching\n  instruction is no longer the same aligned backward branch; update or recover\n  only when EX advances, with redirect taking priority over fetch stalls. The\n  single entry should capture the hottest loop while limiting area and Fmax\n  cost enough for the cycle saving to improve CoreMark iterations per second.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 2\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add the one-entry PC/target predictor, exact-match fetch selection, reset and accepted-EX training or invalidation; preserve redirect priority over stalls.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Carry the predicted successor PC with each fetched and decoded instruction.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch the predicted successor PC only with an accepted instruction.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare predicted and resolved successor PCs, recover on mismatch, and expose valid aligned backward-branch outcomes when EX advances.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect prediction metadata, one-time EX training, and recovery while preserving the nret=1 RVFI interface.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Flush younger work on misprediction and defer recovery and training while EX is blocked by a data-memory stall or divide hold.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Check repeated loop branches, loop exits, stale or changed instructions, misaligned targets, bus stalls, wrong-path suppression, and RVFI PC and order correctness.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
