{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category')=='predictor':\n  print('\\\\n',d['id'],d['title'],'delta',d.get('delta_pct'),'MHz',d.get('fmax_mhz'),'cycles',d.get('cycles'),'LUT',d.get('lut4'))\n  h=d.get('hypothesis')\n  if isinstance(h,dict): h=h.get('hypothesis','')\n  print(str(h)[:2100].replace('\\\\n',' '))\n  print('NOTES:',str(d.get('implementation_notes',''))[:400].replace('\\\\n',' '))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/zsh -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category')=='predictor':\n  print('\\\\n',d['id'],d['title'],'delta',d.get('delta_pct'),'MHz',d.get('fmax_mhz'),'cycles',d.get('cycles'),'LUT',d.get('lut4'))\n  h=d.get('hypothesis')\n  if isinstance(h,dict): h=h.get('hypothesis','')\n  print(str(h)[:2100].replace('\\\\n',' '))\n  print('NOTES:',str(d.get('implementation_notes',''))[:400].replace('\\\\n',' '))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\n hyp-20260923-003-r1s2 Predict control flow with a small branch target buffer delta 23.07 MHz 147.38 cycles 4234052 LUT 10412\nAdd a 16-entry direct-mapped, fully tagged branch target buffer at fetch. Each entry holds a target and a two-bit saturating direction counter; unconditional JAL/JALR entries always predict taken. On a tag miss, fetch proceeds sequentially. Train only when a valid control-flow instruction advances through EX, using its resolved aligned target and outcome. Carry the exact predicted next PC with the instruction into EX, and redirect/flush younger work only when it differs from the resolved next PC. Suppress training and recovery while EX is held by a dmem stall, then perform them when EX advances. Preserve the existing sequential next PC and trap behavior for misaligned targets, and correct stale predictions even if the instruction at a trained PC changes. This should save cycles on recurring CoreMark branches and calls while keeping the added lookup small enough to limit Fmax loss. \nNOTES: \n\n hyp-20260923-003-r2s2 Add a tagged branch target buffer to the iterative-divider core delta -3.58 MHz 142.61 cycles 4234021 LUT 6042\nAdd the previously validated 16-entry direct-mapped, fully tagged branch target buffer to the current iterative-divider pipeline. Store a target and two-bit direction counter per entry; predict trained conditional branches from the counter and JAL/JALR as taken. On a miss, fetch PC+4. Carry the predicted successor PC with each instruction and compare it against the resolved successor in EX. Redirect and flush younger work only on a mismatch, including stale entries for non-control instructions. Train or invalidate only when EX advances, so dmem stalls cannot duplicate updates or lose recovery. Preserve sequential trap behavior for misaligned targets. The divider's LUT reduction should let the measured BTB cycle gain improve fitness without exceeding the area limit. \nNOTES: \n\n hyp-20260923-003-r3s2 Predict direct branches with a direction-only history table delta -3.64 MH\n…[6889 of 9961 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a3b63374191de674]…\ninstruction, target PC, and target successor with the branch into ID/EX. This comparison feeds only metadata flops, never the fetch PC mux.  When EX actually resolves that matching direct branch as taken and advances, use the existing redirect event to inject the cached target instruction into ID/EX with its true target PC. Set the fetch PC to the cached target successor at the same edge. This replaces the redirect bubble with useful work even if the live imem port is stalled. On a miss, untaken branch, invalid instruction, misaligned target, or held EX stage, retain normal redirect and bubble behavior. Capture the target instruction only on an accepted imem response; hold pending training through bus stalls, and copy cache data into ID/EX so an intervening table update cannot change an in-flight replay. Replaying only an already resolved taken branch avoids a direction-misprediction path, while the one-entry storage and off-PC-path tag check aim to keep Fmax loss below the recovered cycle fraction. \nNOTES: \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
