{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/zsh -c \"rg -n 'branch|predict|critical|Fmax|path' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | tail -2\"", "aggregated_output": "24:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260923-002-r8s1\", \"title\": \"Precompute PC-relative control targets in decode\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current EX stage adds the branch or JAL immediate to the PC before\\nselecting a redirect target and computing the retired next PC. Taken\\ncontrol flow is common in CoreMark, and earlier fetch-side predictors\\nlost fitness when they lengthened PC selection. PC and the decoded\\nimmediate are already available in ID, so this adder can cross the\\nexisting ID/EX boundary without adding a stage or a register field.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current EX stage adds the branch or JAL immediate to the PC before\\nselecting a redirect target and computing the retired next PC. Taken\\ncontrol flow is common in CoreMark, and earlier fetch-side predictors\\nlost fitness when they lengthened PC selection. PC and the decoded\\nimmediate are already available in ID, so this adder can cross the\\nexisting ID/EX boundary without adding a stage or a register field.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"For validated BRANCH and JAL instructions, register PC plus the decoded\\nimmediate in the existing ID/EX immediate field. Keep the raw immediate\\nfor JALR, loads, stores, and arithmetic. EX will use the registered\\nabsolute target for BRANCH and JAL, while retaining its forwarded-rs1\\nplus immediate computation for JALR. Preserve EX branch-condition and\\nalignment checks, redirect priority, link writeback, RVFI next-PC and\\ntrap fields, and all bus-stall behavior. This removes the PC-relative\\ntarget adder from EX-to-IF redirect and EX/MEM result timing with no\\nCoreMark cycle penalty or additional target mux in fetch. The ID path\\ngains an adder, so the Fmax benefit is uncertain but directly testable.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute PC plus immediate in ID for legal BRANCH and JAL, and latch that target in the existing ID/EX immediate field; retain raw immediates for other opcodes.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.\n…[6884 of 9956 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b0a14e0349f47c5b]…\nscription\": \"Let a valid replay replace the usual redirect and imem-stall bubble while preserving load-use and dmem/divider holds.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Check first-visit fill, warm taken loops, untaken exits, JAL, changed branch words, bus stalls, wrong-path side effects, and RVFI order/PC continuity.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 252.03, \"delta_pct\": -38.31, \"vs_baseline\": -10.89, \"fmax_mhz\": 107.4, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4261396, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5809, \"ff\": 2531, \"seeds\": [109.77, 107.4, 105.97], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-23T18:17:26.040448Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 8, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-23 hyp-20260923-003-r8s2 (regression, -38.31%): Even replay after a resolved branch can lose fitness when EX-qualified cached-instruction and successor muxes feed IF/ID in the same cycle; roughly 5% fewer CoreMark cycles could not offset Fmax falling from 183.52 to 107.4 MHz.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
